  <main>
    <p>I found a lantern hanging from a branch. Under it sat a fox with a pencil behind its ear.</p>

    <p>“You left this part empty,” the fox said.</p>

    <p>“I had not thought of anything yet.”</p>

    <p>“Empty is not the same as finished.”</p>

    <p>Behind the fox, the forest faded into white paper. I could draw whatever I wanted there. A castle. A monster. An entire second world. For a moment, I wanted to add everything.</p>

    <p>Then I noticed a single set of footprints leading toward the village. Someone had walked through this unfinished forest without waiting for me to make it perfect.</p>

    <p>The fox offered me the lantern. “What do you want to see first?”</p>

